cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these model files, please cite this archive, the SuperSLIM package and the data sources listed in ATTRIBUTION.md."
type: dataset
title: "SuperSLIM models: trained model files built from data with verified terms"
authors:
  - family-names: Kumakura
    given-names: Daiki
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9859-0720"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24395561"
version: "4.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-21"
license: CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/DaikiKumakura/superslim/tree/main/models"
abstract: >-
  Trained model files for the SuperSLIM package. superslim_open_v4.npz predicts the mean transcriptome response to knocking down a gene in K562, HCT116, HEK293T, primary CD4+ T cells, KOLF2.1J iPSC, and RPE1, Jurkat and HepG2 essential-gene screens, and was trained only on data whose terms were verified. Non-commercial use (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0).
keywords:
  - "Perturb-seq"
  - "CRISPRi"
  - "perturbation response"
references:
